<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sixteen Kingdoms</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sixteen Kingdoms was a period of Chinese history in the fourth and fifth centuries CE, when northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> was divided among many short-lived states, many founded by non-Chinese peoples. The migration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-xiongnu">Southern Xiongnu</a> into China contributed to this period. Several of these states were founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> leaders.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Eastern Jin preserved the legitimacy, institutions and high culture of the Han and Jin world in the south while northern China was divided among the <b>Sixteen Kingdoms</b>, and in doing so began the long shift of China's population and economic centre towards the Yangtze.</blockquote><a href="/empire/eastern-jin">Eastern Jin · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…the Tiefu-led Helian Xia in 426 and took its capital Tongwancheng in 427; the Northern Liang in the Hexi Corridor submitted as a vassal, the Northern Yan fell in 436, and in 439 Taiwu conquered the Northern Liang outright, uniting the north and closing the <b>Sixteen Kingdoms</b> period.</blockquote><a href="/empire/northern-wei">Northern Wei · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the Southern Xiongnu settled within the Chinese frontier, contributing to the transformation of northern China that culminated in the <b>Sixteen Kingdoms</b> period of the fourth and fifth centuries, when Liu Yuan, a Xiongnu noble, founded the Han Zhao state in 304, and his successors sacked Luoyang in 311.</blockquote><a href="/empire/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In 304 Liu Yuan, a descendant of the shanyus, founded Han Zhao, the first of the <b>Sixteen Kingdoms</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/southern-xiongnu">Southern Xiongnu</a></li></ul></section>
